# Proposal page fit (A4 blocks)

These are fixed A4 sheet proposals (`.page` = one printed page). Content is stacked as **whole blocks** (a section, table, card group, step list, CTA, etc.).

## Packing rule

1. Place blocks **under each other** in reading order.
2. If the **entire block fits** in the remaining space on the current page → keep it on that page.
3. If the block would be **cut or split** across pages → move the **whole block** to the next page. Never leave half a section on one page and half on the next.
4. Pack **tight**: put as many whole blocks on a page as fit. Do not leave a page sparse just to isolate one short section, and do not force two blocks onto one page if either would overflow or clip (`overflow: hidden` on `.page`).

## Do / don't

```html
<!-- ✅ GOOD: two whole sections on one page when both fit -->
<div class="page">
  <div class="page-body">
    <div class="section">… Identity …</div>
    <div class="section">… Services …</div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ❌ BAD: one section clipped mid-list / mid-table across page edge -->
<div class="page">… first half of Studio steps …</div>
<div class="page">… remaining Studio steps …</div>
```

## When editing

- In `etkan-culture`, keep each whole unit as a `.content-block` inside `#pack-source`. `shared/pack.js` stacks them under each other: keep on the current page if the whole block fits, otherwise start a new page. Do not hard-split one section across two `.page` sheets by hand.
- Cover pages stay alone; do not pack content onto `page-cover`.
- After changing blocks, reload and confirm pages are packed (not one short section per page) and nothing is clipped.

## Shared assets

Page chrome, fonts, toolbar and PDF export live in `shared/`. A new proposal links them and sets its own config; only content and proposal-specific rules go in the folder's own `style.css`.

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../shared/base.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
...
<script>
  window.PROPOSAL = {
    filename: "Deck-Name.pdf",
    footerBrand: "ETKAN",
    packReady: "__etkanPackReady",
    coverBg: "#171B2E",
    pageBg: "#EDF2F5"
  };
</script>
<script src="../shared/pack.js"></script>
<script src="../shared/export.js"></script>
```

Omit `pack.js`, `footerBrand` and `packReady` for decks whose `.page` sheets are laid out by hand. `telecel-proposal` keeps its own theme CSS and only uses `shared/export.js`.
